causal-loop 1
title "What impacts the cod population in the UK"

# What impacts the cod population in the UK.
#
# Redrawn from "Diagram 7: CLD telling the story of what impacts cod population
# in the UK" in: Avanthika Kamath, Freya Ivy Palmer, Imali Manikarachchige and
# Craig Hutton (2024). Causal Loop Diagram. National Centre for Research
# Methods online learning resource, University of Southampton.
# https://repository.ncrm.ac.uk/resources/online/all/causal_loop-diagram
# (accessed 31 October 2026). The figure is © the authors and the National
# Centre for Research Methods; no licence is stated, and it is redrawn here as
# a cited academic source. SOURCE.md beside this file says more.
#
# The figure is handwritten. Its labels are transcribed in its own words, and
# where the handwriting is unclear they are read against the page's own text,
# Diagrams 3 to 6 (the four parts Diagram 7 joins) and the transcripts of the
# two videos. A variable the figure writes twice, once in grey as a reminder
# (consumer demand, the hospitality sector and the recruitment rate), is one
# variable here.
#
# The figure prints a polarity on nearly every arrow. The few it leaves bare
# stay bare, except where the arrow plainly means one: those carry it and the
# note "not printed". Carrying capacity, the tipping point, is joined by double
# arrows with delay marks and no polarity; the page says it behaves one way
# until a threshold is reached and another after it, so no fixed polarity is
# added, and every loop through it is undecidable. Nothing is simulated.
#
# The figure marks twelve loops with R or B. Nine are named first below with
# the figure's own letter, and four of those letters disagree with the arrows'
# arithmetic: ADP reports them and changes nothing, as it should. The other
# three marks (an R beside legal fishing grounds, an R between employment and
# the processing industry, and a B below consumer price) cannot be tied to one
# cycle with confidence and are not assigned. Every other cycle the arrows make
# is named after them, labelled by its arithmetic.

# ---- variables ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Environment.
variable temperature "Temperature"
variable salinity "Salinity"
variable habitat "Habitat"
variable season "Season"
variable spawning "Spawning"
variable birthRate "Birth rate"
variable juvenileCod "Juvenile cod fish population"
variable recruitmentRate "Recruitment rate"
variable adultCod "Adult cod population"
variable crustaceans "Crustacean population"
variable juvenileMortality "Mortality rate"
variable otherMortalityFactor "Other mortality factor"
variable otherMortalityRate "Other mortality rate"
variable fishingMortality "Fishing mortality rate"
variable predationMortality "Predation mortality rate"
variable dogfish "Dog fish population"
variable marineMammals "Marine mammal population"
variable sharks "Shark population"

# Tipping point.
variable carryingCapacity "Carrying capacity"

# Social.
variable tourism "Tourism"
variable fishingVillages "Fishing villages"
variable fishingActivity "Fishing activity"
variable employment "Employment"
variable processingIndustry "Processing industry"
variable supplyChain "Supply chain"
variable hospitalitySector "Hospitality sector"
variable consumerDemand "Consumer demand"
variable healthNutrition "Health & nutrition"
variable domesticConsumption "Domestic consumption"

# Economic.
variable localEconomy "Local economy"
variable localInfrastructure "Local infrastructure"
variable supply "Supply"
variable marketPrice "Market price"
variable worldPrice "World price"
variable localPrice "Local price"
variable priceGap "Price gap"
variable exports "Exports"
variable imports "Imports"
variable consumerPrice "Consumer price"
variable tradeGap "Trade gap"
variable profit "Profit"
variable cost "Cost"
variable income "Income"

# Regulation.
variable hpmaMpa "HPMA/MPA"
variable legalFishingGrounds "Legal fishing grounds"
variable closureZones "Closure zones/times"
variable gearRestrictions "Gear restrictions"
variable surveyResults "Population survey results"
variable quotaTac "Quota/TAC"

# ---- environment -------------------------------------------------------------
# Spawning conditions set the birth rate; juveniles are recruited into the adult
# population, which spawns. Both eat crustaceans, adults eat juveniles, and
# predators, fishing and other causes take adults.

link temperature -> spawning
link salinity -> spawning
link habitat -> spawning + "not printed"
link season -> spawning
link spawning -> birthRate +
link birthRate -> juvenileCod +
link juvenileCod -> recruitmentRate +
link recruitmentRate -> adultCod +
link adultCod -> spawning +
link juvenileCod -> crustaceans -
link adultCod -> crustaceans -
link crustaceans -> recruitmentRate +
link adultCod -> juvenileMortality + "adult cod eat juvenile cod"
link juvenileMortality -> juvenileCod - "not drawn: the first video's transcript states it"
link otherMortalityFactor -> juvenileMortality +
link otherMortalityFactor -> otherMortalityRate +
link otherMortalityRate -> adultCod -
link fishingMortality -> adultCod -
link predationMortality -> adultCod -
link dogfish -> predationMortality +
link marineMammals -> predationMortality +
link sharks -> predationMortality +

# ---- tipping point -----------------------------------------------------------
# Drawn with delay marks and no polarity: a threshold, not a direction.

link spawning -> carryingCapacity delayed
link carryingCapacity -> spawning delayed
link crustaceans -> carryingCapacity delayed
link adultCod -> carryingCapacity delayed
link carryingCapacity -> adultCod delayed

# ---- social ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seals, sharks and fishing villages draw tourists. Fishing activity employs
# people and feeds the processing industry, the supply chain, the hospitality
# sector and domestic consumption, which return as consumer demand.

link marineMammals -> tourism +
link sharks -> tourism +
link fishingVillages -> tourism +
link fishingActivity -> fishingVillages +
link fishingActivity -> fishingMortality +
link fishingActivity -> employment +
link fishingActivity -> processingIndustry +
link processingIndustry -> employment +
link processingIndustry -> supplyChain +
link supplyChain -> processingIndustry +
link supplyChain -> hospitalitySector +
link supplyChain -> domesticConsumption +
link hospitalitySector -> consumerDemand +
link healthNutrition -> hospitalitySector +
link healthNutrition -> domesticConsumption +
link domesticConsumption -> consumerDemand +
link consumerDemand -> fishingActivity +

# ---- economic ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Tourism builds the local economy and its infrastructure. The catch and
# consumer demand make the supply; supply lowers the market price, which sets
# the world and local prices, the profit and, through the consumer price, the
# demand again.

link tourism -> localEconomy +
link localEconomy -> localInfrastructure +
link localInfrastructure -> hospitalitySector +
link localInfrastructure -> fishingVillages +
link localInfrastructure -> employment +
link employment -> income +
link profit -> income +
link profit -> fishingActivity +
link cost -> profit -
link marketPrice -> profit +
link fishingActivity -> supply +
link consumerDemand -> supply +
link supply -> marketPrice -
link marketPrice -> worldPrice +
link marketPrice -> localPrice +
link worldPrice -> localPrice + "not printed: a double arrow"
link localPrice -> worldPrice + "not printed: a double arrow"
link worldPrice -> priceGap
link localPrice -> priceGap
link worldPrice -> exports -
link localPrice -> imports +
link localPrice -> consumerPrice +
link consumerPrice -> consumerDemand -
link exports -> tradeGap
link imports -> tradeGap

# ---- regulation --------------------------------------------------------------
# Protected areas, closures and gear restrictions limit the legal fishing
# grounds; surveys of the adult population set the quota, the total allowable
# catch.

link hpmaMpa -> habitat +
link hpmaMpa -> legalFishingGrounds -
link closureZones -> legalFishingGrounds -
link gearRestrictions -> legalFishingGrounds -
link closureZones -> recruitmentRate +
link gearRestrictions -> recruitmentRate +
link legalFishingGrounds -> habitat -
link legalFishingGrounds -> fishingActivity +
link fishingMortality -> legalFishingGrounds + "read as drawn: the arrow leaves the fishing mortality rate"
link adultCod -> surveyResults +
link surveyResults -> quotaTac +
link quotaTac -> fishingActivity +

# ---- the loops the figure marks ----------------------------------------------
# With the figure's own letter. R2, R3, B2 and B3 disagree with their arrows:
# the figure, and for R2 the first video's transcript, call them what the
# letter says, and ADP reports the difference rather than choosing a side.

loop R1 "Cod spawn cod" spawning birthRate juvenileCod recruitmentRate adultCod
loop B1 "Adults eat their own food" adultCod crustaceans recruitmentRate
loop R2 "Adults eat the young" adultCod juvenileMortality juvenileCod recruitmentRate
loop R3 "Surveys set the quota" adultCod surveyResults quotaTac fishingActivity fishingMortality
loop B2 "Fishing and the legal grounds" legalFishingGrounds fishingActivity fishingMortality
loop B3 "Price balances supply and demand" consumerDemand supply marketPrice localPrice consumerPrice
loop R4 "Tourism builds the coast" tourism localEconomy localInfrastructure fishingVillages
loop R5 "Demand drives the catch" consumerDemand fishingActivity processingIndustry supplyChain hospitalitySector
loop R6 "Processing and supply feed each other" processingIndustry supplyChain

# ---- the other cycles the arrows make -----------------------------------------
# Named so that every cycle is claimed, labelled by its arithmetic. The T loops
# run through carrying capacity, claim no polarity and are undecidable.

loop R7 "World and local prices move together" worldPrice localPrice
loop R8 "Fewer young leave more food" crustaceans recruitmentRate adultCod juvenileMortality juvenileCod
loop R9 "World price feeds the consumer price" marketPrice worldPrice localPrice consumerPrice consumerDemand supply
loop R10 "Dear fish, less fishing" marketPrice localPrice consumerPrice consumerDemand fishingActivity supply
loop R11 "Infrastructure feeds demand" tourism localEconomy localInfrastructure hospitalitySector consumerDemand fishingActivity fishingVillages
loop R12 "World price and the catch" marketPrice worldPrice localPrice consumerPrice consumerDemand fishingActivity supply
loop R13 "Domestic consumption drives the catch" supplyChain domesticConsumption consumerDemand fishingActivity processingIndustry
loop R14 "Quota, grounds, habitat and food" surveyResults quotaTac fishingActivity fishingMortality legalFishingGrounds habitat spawning birthRate juvenileCod crustaceans recruitmentRate adultCod
loop B4 "The catch lowers its own price" marketPrice profit fishingActivity supply
loop B5 "Young cod eat the adults' food" spawning birthRate juvenileCod crustaceans recruitmentRate adultCod
loop B6 "Profit, hospitality and demand" marketPrice profit fishingActivity processingIndustry supplyChain hospitalitySector consumerDemand supply
loop B7 "Profit, consumption and demand" marketPrice profit fishingActivity processingIndustry supplyChain domesticConsumption consumerDemand supply
loop B8 "Profit, tourism and demand" tourism localEconomy localInfrastructure hospitalitySector consumerDemand supply marketPrice profit fishingActivity fishingVillages
loop B9 "Quota, grounds and spawning habitat" surveyResults quotaTac fishingActivity fishingMortality legalFishingGrounds habitat spawning birthRate juvenileCod recruitmentRate adultCod
loop T1 "Spawning and carrying capacity" spawning carryingCapacity
loop T2 "Adult cod and carrying capacity" carryingCapacity adultCod
loop T3 "Adults, carrying capacity and spawning" spawning carryingCapacity adultCod
loop T4 "Food and carrying capacity" crustaceans carryingCapacity adultCod
loop T5 "Young cod, food and carrying capacity" spawning birthRate juvenileCod crustaceans carryingCapacity
loop T6 "Eaten young, food and carrying capacity" crustaceans carryingCapacity adultCod juvenileMortality juvenileCod
loop T7 "Recruitment and carrying capacity" spawning birthRate juvenileCod recruitmentRate adultCod carryingCapacity
loop T8 "Young cod's food and carrying capacity" spawning birthRate juvenileCod crustaceans carryingCapacity adultCod
loop T9 "Adults' food and carrying capacity" spawning birthRate juvenileCod recruitmentRate adultCod crustaceans carryingCapacity
loop T10 "Food, recruitment and carrying capacity" spawning birthRate juvenileCod crustaceans recruitmentRate adultCod carryingCapacity
loop T11 "Quota, habitat and carrying capacity" surveyResults quotaTac fishingActivity fishingMortality legalFishingGrounds habitat spawning carryingCapacity adultCod
loop T12 "Quota, food and carrying capacity" surveyResults quotaTac fishingActivity fishingMortality legalFishingGrounds habitat spawning birthRate juvenileCod crustaceans carryingCapacity adultCod
